From 6208a29df8af9484154f9c1f45c14ca8ead98aae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yami <yamiemail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Mar 2026 18:59:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: shadow table API via direct KernelPatch supercall

Add gum_yszint_shadow_register/unregister API for registering
original bytes with yszint-stealth KPM. Uses direct syscall(45)
to KernelPatch supercall ABI instead of fork/exec kpatch binary.

New files:
- gum/gumyszintshadow.h: Public API header
- gum/gumyszintshadow.c: Implementation with direct supercall

JS bindings:
- Interceptor.enableShadow(superkey): Initialize with KPM superkey
- Interceptor.registerShadow(target, originalBytes): Register shadow
- Interceptor.removeShadow(target): Remove shadow entry
- Interceptor.shadowEnabled: Check if KPM shadow is available

The shadow system sends original pre-hook bytes to the KPM so
kernel-level /proc/[pid]/mem reads return untouched code, defeating
integrity checks that read memory via syscall.
